      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add Claw status and remove lifecycle",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nFinal OpenClaw PR in the current Claws stack. This adds the first supported lifecycle management commands over the state produced by the mutating apply PRs:\n\n- `claws status [claw] --json` reports persisted Claw apply records, plugin artifact refs, and workspace file refs\n- `claws remove <claw> --dry-run --json` previews removal without deleting files or refs\n- `claws remove <claw> --yes --json` removes persisted Claw refs and deletes unchanged Claw-managed workspace files\n- user-modified, oversized, missing, or already-deleted workspace files are retained or treated as stale cleanup instead of being deleted unsafely\n- workspace removal preflights all refs before deleting any file, revalidates the managed hash immediately before unlinking, and keeps failed refs visible in status on partial cleanup errors\n- artifact refs are removed as Claw provenance only; this does not uninstall plugin packages\n\n## Stack\n\n- RFC: openclaw/rfcs#27\n- Validation/dry-run foundation: #101328\n- Artifact provenance refs: #101755\n- Workspace/persona files apply: #101973\n- Plugin artifact installers + warning provenance: #102228\n- This PR: Claw status/remove lifecycle\n\n## Behavior Notes\n\nThis intentionally stops short of update, rollback, automation/crons, skill/MCP/connectors installers, and ClawHub discovery. It gives users an end-to-end supported lifecycle for the state that the current stack can already create: apply, inspect persisted state, preview removal, remove Claw-owned metadata, and clean unchanged managed workspace files.\n\n`claws remove` does not ref-count-lock or uninstall plugins. It removes Claw refs so future plugin uninstall warnings no longer include the removed Claw.\n\n## Real Behavior Proof\n\nThe E2E suite now runs a full real CLI lifecycle using `node --import tsx src/entry.ts`:\n\n1. apply a local plugin Claw with `--yes --workspace --json`\n2. verify `claws status <id> --json` reports artifact and workspace refs\n3. verify `claws remove <id> --dry-run --json` previews workspace deletion without deleting the file\n4. run `claws remove <id> --yes --json`\n5. verify the managed workspace file is deleted\n6. verify final `claws status <id> --json` is empty\n\n## Validation\n\nRun on WSL worktree `/root/src/openclaw-claws-pr6-lifecycle` at head `49eb30ad775269f7ad48e7817a1cc4c45acb70c6`:\n\n```text\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/claws/schema.test.ts src/claws/provenance.test.ts src/claws/artifact-installers.test.ts src/claws/workspace.test.ts src/claws/lifecycle-state.test.ts src/state/openclaw-state-db.test.ts src/cli/claws-cli.test.ts src/cli/plugins-cli.uninstall.test.ts src/claws/lifecycle.e2e.test.ts src/cli/program/command-registry.test.ts src/cli/program/root-command-descriptions.test.ts\n```\n\nResult: passed 3 Vitest shards: unit 84 tests, CLI 42 tests, lifecycle E2E 5 tests.\n\n```text\ngit diff --check\nnode scripts/check-no-conflict-markers.mjs\n```\n\nResult: passed.\n\n```text\npnpm exec tsgo --noEmit --pretty false\n```\n\nResult: still blocked only by existing unrelated baseline:\n\n```text\nsrc/secrets/config-io.ts(12,17): error TS4058: Return type of exported function has or is using name 'configWritePostCommitRollback' from external module \"/root/src/openclaw-claws-pr6-lifecycle/src/config/io\" but cannot be named.\n```\n\n```text\ncodex review -c model=gpt-5.5 --base origin/user/giodl/claws-pr5-installers\n```\n\nResult: no actionable correctness issues found after fixes for review findings around stale workspace roots, partial delete preflight, hash revalidation, delete errors, and oversized modified files.\n",
